        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Zoids VS II",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "The release of Zoids VS II brought about several improvements to the game, including better landscape graphics, more Zoids, and a new user-interface. It also featured the new fist mode, engaging players at close-quarters combat. Released in Japan on September 4, 2003. The game included a variety of pilots, Zoids, weapons, and parts. Over 50 pilots were available to play as, including characters from Zoids: New Century and Chaotic Century. A large number of Zoids were included in the game including more than 60 Zoids and secret unlockable Zoids. By using a memory card containing data from the original Zoids VS, a Shield Liger DCS-J was available in the shop, which was otherwise unusable.\n\nZoids Battle Legends\nThe English dub of Zoids VS II, it featured a complete translation of the other game, albeit with a few errors. Brad is named \"Ballad,\" Thomas is called \"Thoma\", Blood is named \"Brad\", etc.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "2003",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
